{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Securities Commission - Aerie Exchange{% endblock %}

{% block meta %}
	<meta name="description" content="The District's Securities Commission: who heads it, the margin investors put up, and what listed companies must disclose.">
	<meta property="og:title" content="Securities Commission | Aerie Exchange">
	<meta property="og:type" content="website">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="max-w-400 mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-12 w-full space-y-6">

	{% include 'government/_breadcrumb.html.twig' with {current: 'Securities Commission'} %}
	<header class="pb-5 border-b border-outline-variant/15">
		<h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-on-surface tracking-tight">Securities Commission</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
			Sets the rules of the Aerie Exchange. Its head is named by the Aerie Council for a single term and decides the
			margin an investor must put up to buy or short on credit, and how hard the Commission pursues listed companies
			that dress up their results.
		</p>
	</header>

	{% if commission %}
		{% set head = commission.head %}
		{% set rules = commission.inForce %}
		<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="head-heading">
			<h2 id="head-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The head</h2>
			<p class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface mt-2">{{ head.name }}</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-0.5">Age {{ head.age }} · seated {{ head.sinceLabel }} · term ends <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ head.termEndsLabel }}</span></p>
			<p class="text-sm text-on-surface mt-2 max-w-3xl">
				{%- if head.opening -%}
					Keeps the rules the Exchange had at Year 1
				{%- else -%}
					{{ {light: 'A light-touch overseer of the markets', balanced: 'Takes a middle course', strict: 'A strict overseer of the markets'}[head.stance] }}
				{%- endif -%}
				{%- if head.passedOver is not empty %}, chosen over {% for candidate in head.passedOver %}{{ candidate.name }} <span class="text-on-surface-variant">(margin <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ candidate.margin|pct(0) }}</span>, {{ candidate.age }})</span>{{ loop.last ? '' : (loop.revindex == 2 ? ' and ' : ', ') }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}.
			</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-2 max-w-3xl">
				The Council names the head for a single {{ commission.rules.termYears|number_format(0) }}-year term from a shortlist of {{ commission.rules.shortlist }}, choosing the candidate nearest its own view of the markets.
				A new head's rules take effect {{ commission.rules.noticeMonths }} months after they are seated.
				{% if commission.councilMargin is not null %}The Council's median member would set the initial margin at <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.councilMargin|pct(0) }}</span>.{% endif %}
			</p>
			{% if commission.coming %}
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-3 max-w-3xl">
					From <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.coming.fromLabel }}</span>: initial margin <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.coming.initial|pct(0) }}</span>, and companies left <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.coming.enforcement|pct(0) }}</span> of the room they had at Year 1 to steer their results.
				</p>
			{% endif %}
		</section>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="margin-heading">
				<h2 id="margin-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Buying on credit</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ rules.initial|pct(0) }}</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">initial margin: the equity a new position needs, as a share of its value</p>
				<dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mt-4 text-xs">
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Maintenance on longs</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ rules.long|pct(0) }}</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Maintenance on shorts</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ rules.short|pct(0) }}</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-4 leading-relaxed">
					A higher initial margin lets an account borrow less against what it holds; it never calls a position already open.
					Maintenance is the line below which a broker calls the account, and it does not move with the head.
					A head may set the initial margin anywhere from <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.rules.lightestMargin|pct(0) }}</span> to <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.rules.strictestMargin|pct(0) }}</span>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="disclosure-heading">
				<h2 id="disclosure-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">Honest results</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ rules.enforcement|pct(0) }}</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">of the room companies had at Year 1 to steer their reported earnings onto the forecast</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					A company a little short of the forecast can book revenue early or a provision light and print a meet or a one-cent beat.
					What it borrows that way is paid back out of later quarters. The harder the Commission pursues it, the fewer companies try.
					A head may leave companies anywhere from <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.rules.strictestEnforcement|pct(0) }}</span> to <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ commission.rules.lightestEnforcement|pct(0) }}</span> of that room.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	{% else %}
		<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">The Securities Commission has no head yet.</p>
	{% endif %}

	<p class="source-note">{{ source_line('securities-commission') }}</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
